      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Rubio visits Rome amid deepening Italy-US rift over Iran war, Hormuz, and troop withdrawal threat",
      "summary": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio made a two-day Rome visit (May 7-8), meeting Foreign Minister Tajani at the Farnesina and Premier Meloni at Palazzo Chigi for roughly 90 minutes each. The meetings were framed as diplomatic repair after Trump's public attacks on Italy for refusing to support US-Israeli operations against Iran and for denying use of the Sigonella base; Trump subsequently told Corriere della Sera he was still considering withdrawing US troops. Tajani announced a 'Rome Coalition' on Hormuz food-security and indicated Italy could deploy minesweepers after a ceasefire; Meloni described the talks as 'frank' while stressing national interest; parliament scheduled a joint foreign/defence committee hearing on Hormuz for May 13. Opposition leaders and analysts characterized the meeting as inconclusive.",
